# Teller integration rules

## Adapter pattern

- `src/lib/accounting/` = core (provider-agnostic).
- `src/lib/integrations/<provider>.ts` = maps external payloads → core posting/import functions.
- Do not embed Stripe/HFAC/Plaid logic inside invoice or expense routes.

## HFAC webhooks

Routes under `src/app/api/integrations/hfac/`:

- Auth: `Authorization: Bearer TELLER_HFAC_WEBHOOK_SECRET`
- Use `createServiceClient()` + explicit `organizationId` in body
- Idempotent imports (check `external_id`, payment intent dedupe)
- Record delivery via `recordHfacWebhookDelivery()`

## External identifiers

- `external_source`: use `HFAC_EXTERNAL_SOURCE` from `constants.ts`
- `external_id`: stable provider key for upsert/dedupe

## Payment data

Store amounts, dates, Stripe/HFAC reference IDs — never PAN, CVV, or bank login credentials.

## New providers

Add adapter module + webhook route + env docs in README — do not couple to HFAC code paths.
